@startuml fig2_states
' Diagram 2 of the VDI 3682 pattern: the states a process moves.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: the three kinds of state a process moves, and how an operator
' takes them in and puts them out.
'
' The dependency is drawn alongside the two. It ties one state to another
' without anything passing between them, as a piece of information is bound to
' the product it describes, and it is what holds the branches of a parallel run
' together.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - process structure and decomposition: diagram 1
'  - the flow carrying a state between two elements: diagram 3, which needs the
'    room because four source and target relations run between the same classes
'  - resources and their assignment: diagram 4

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

' ===================================================================
'  The three kinds of state
' ===================================================================

class State
class Product
class Energy
class Information

State <|-- Product
State <|-- Energy
State <|-- Information

' ===================================================================
'  What an operator consumes and produces
' ===================================================================

class ProcessOperator

' Two parallel edges between the same classes. Given the same direction their
' labels stack, so they are routed to opposite sides of the operator. The
' pattern declares no inverse for either, so both keep the name a model states.
ProcessOperator --> "*" State : hasInput
ProcessOperator --> "*" State : hasOutput

State --> "*" State : dependency

' Layout only: the operator above the state, the three kinds below it, so the
' three generalisations stay separate lines rather than merging into one.
ProcessOperator -[hidden]down- State
Product -[hidden]right- Energy
Energy  -[hidden]right- Information

@enduml
